🧠 Core Principle

A "skill" is any unlockable unit:

Alankar

Song phrase

Full song

Future gamified drill

Advanced technique module

Everything becomes:

(user_id, skill_id) → progression state
🗄 Canonical Table: skill_progress
CREATE TABLE skill_progress (
    user_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    skill_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    skill_type TEXT NOT NULL,   -- "alankar" | "phrase" | "song" | "technique"

    successful_sessions INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    total_sessions INTEGER DEFAULT 0,

    composite_average REAL DEFAULT 0.0,
    recent_weighted_average REAL DEFAULT 0.0,

    last_composite_score REAL,
    last_session_at TEXT,
    last_success_at TEXT,

    is_unlocked BOOLEAN DEFAULT 0,
    unlocked_at TEXT,

    PRIMARY KEY (user_id, skill_id),

    CHECK (NOT (is_unlocked = 1 AND unlocked_at IS NULL)),
    CHECK (NOT (is_unlocked = 0 AND unlocked_at IS NOT NULL))
);
🔑 Why This Design Is Correct
1️⃣ Skill-Type Agnostic

No separate mastery tables.
No branching logic.
Curriculum engine queries by skill_type.

2️⃣ Forward-Only Unlock Built-In

Unlock rule:

if successful_sessions >= 3 and not is_unlocked:
    is_unlocked = True
    unlocked_at = now()

Never reversed.
Constraint enforced at DB level.

3️⃣ Analytics Integrated

Instead of computing composite history repeatedly:

Store rolling weighted average.

Store last composite.

Store success count.

This allows:

Quick difficulty recommendation.

Trend-based gating.

Future AI-driven adaptation.

