PART 2 — Clean Streak Domain Model

Now we design streak properly — not helper-level.

🎯 Design Goal

Timezone-safe

Idempotent per logical day

No double increment

No server midnight issues

Offset-adjustable

Travel-safe

🗄 Tables
1️⃣ user_profile
CREATE TABLE user_profile (
    user_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    timezone_offset_minutes INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    created_at TEXT DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    updated_at TEXT DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);
2️⃣ practice_streak
CREATE TABLE practice_streak (
    user_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,

    current_streak INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    longest_streak INTEGER DEFAULT 0,

    last_practice_logical_date TEXT,
    total_practice_days INTEGER DEFAULT 0,

    updated_at TEXT DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);
🧠 Core Concept

We NEVER use server date directly.

We use:

logical_date = utc_now + user_timezone_offset

Everything is computed on logical_date.

🔁 Canonical Update Function
def update_practice_streak(user_id: str) -> dict:
Flow:

Compute logical_date

Fetch last_practice_logical_date

Calculate delta_days

If:

delta == 0 → no change

delta == 1 → increment streak

delta > 1 → reset to 1

no previous record → set to 1

Update longest_streak if needed

Save atomic

🛡 Idempotency Guarantee

If same user submits 3 sessions same day:

delta = 0
Streak unchanged.

No double increment possible.

📦 Optional Enhancement (Future-Proof)

Add:

CREATE TABLE practice_days (
    user_id TEXT,
    logical_date TEXT,
    PRIMARY KEY (user_id, logical_date)
);

Then:

Insert logical_date

If conflict → already practiced

Streak increments only when new row inserted

This gives perfect dedupe.

